The Environmental and Water Practitioners' Association (ENVASS) is a not-for-profit association of practicing environmental and water professionals who are committed to the development of the environmental and water law and practice in South Africa. The association promotes environmental and water law and practice by facilitating the exchange of ideas, information and best practice, and by promoting environmental and water law as an important element in sustainable development. The association is governed by an elected board of directors composed of practicing environmental and water professionals who have experience and expertise in this area. The association encourages participation by legal professionals and other stakeholders, and promotes networking among members. It holds annual conferences and workshops to foster learning and professional development. It also provides members with a platform to share information and experiences.
